# Sketch line/diamond stage

This isolated stage adds usable plain two-point **Line** and **Diamond** tools to
the frozen Sketch baseline. Draw, select, move, resize, group, undo/redo, save/load,
SVG and native `.excalidraw` projection work with the new types. Reverse line
drags preserve signed endpoint directions. Diamond painting and hit selection use
the same bounded polygon, excluding the rectangle's corners. Existing freehand,
group and native unknown-field behavior stays covered by the original tests.

Production was copied before work to `production-baseline/`; its exact 11-file
source/evidence/store-dependency manifest is `production-baseline-manifest.json`.
No production, shared host, prior stage/history, package or registry was edited.

The source-assisted MIT bindings are in `source-provenance.json` and
`THIRD-PARTY-NOTICE.md`. Exact official npm archive, emitted bundle and source-map
digests were authenticated; the map entry matched the official archive. Four
retained source files bind linear types/restoration/point size and diamond bounds.
Twenty-five unchanged original helper slices carry byte offsets, lines and hashes.
The application never executes original vendor helpers. Test-only VMs compare
eight signed line configurations and eight diamond dimensions/restorations plus
original local serializer roundtrip; unknown native fields and negative imported
diamond canonicalization are covered separately.

The additional diamond helper follows original `floor(size/2)+1` anchors for normal
dimensions. Sub-pixel/degenerate dimensions clamp those anchors within editable
bounds; this differs from upstream and is warned/documented. Polygon interiors are
selectable even when no fill is painted, consistent with this editor's geometric
selection; original transparent-shape hit semantics were not compared. Native diamond raw
negative dimensions stay untouched until geometry editing, when canonical positive
dimensions are exported once. Line-head metadata stays preserved with a warning
but no painted heads. Curved/multi-point/bound linear elements, rotated/locked
objects, images and unsupported types remain inert native records. Rough rendering,
pressure rendering, bindings repair, polygon editing, rotation, snapping, typography,
collaboration and full original UI behavior remain gaps. Existing 4MiB native JSON,
2,000 elements/shapes, 5,000 freehand points/text characters, coordinate magnitude
1,000,000 and other editor limits are retained. No full parity, renderer pixel
equivalence, security certification or performance-superiority claim is made.

From the workspace root, run `node work/sketch-geometry-next/verify-stage.mjs` for
the complete focused slice. `node work/sketch-geometry-next/preview.mjs` starts a
private loopback preview on an ephemeral port; its records stay in `preview-data`.
The actual browser proof/observations cover negative line drawing, diamond hit
selection, freehand, grouping, undo/redo, group dragging, Save, page reload and Load.
The private browser tab/host were closed after capturing unchanged JPEG proof.
Original full-app rendering and native import/export through original UI were not
claimed; original helper comparisons and API persistence are separate evidence.

Failure history remains under `failures/`: a reference-preparation assumption
about erased type-only map content (fixed using exact official commit types),
two client-test harness errors (a string passed to assert.match and incorrect
assumption of a25px native viewport; fixed assertions/coordinates with unchanged
runtime), one documentation patch validation failure, and a clipped screenshot
timeout (full native screenshot succeeded). Exact available failed source/raw
output is retained. No compression/performance threshold or behavior assertion
was relaxed. Earlier passing runs and original production receipt bytes remain
historical; the final receipt binds the actual final source.

For integration, runtime changes are in `apps/sketch/core.mjs` and `client.mjs`;
the server API and shared storage source are unchanged. The stage adds two focused
test files. Original-oracle paths and new test evidence/fixture output paths are
stage-specific and must be adapted to an app-owned evidence location during
integration, then tests and receipts regenerated. Preserve MIT attribution and
older receipt/source snapshots instead of reattributing them to new production
bytes. The preview host is a test harness, not a production host replacement.
